;; First boot on a Rock Pi 4B Plus (RK3399), headless: does the board boot,
;; take an address from the router, and let us in?
;;
;; Derived from Buildroot's rock4se_defconfig with the DTS and U-Boot
;; board name changed to the 4B Plus, imported and round-tripped by
;; silt import. SSH is added here so there is a way in without a serial
;; cable. The root password is the development one; this is a bench image.

(image rock-pi-4b-plus-bringup
  (compose
    image:rock-pi-4b-plus
    feature:ssh)
  (verified-against (buildroot "2025.02.16")))
